Z||000005||Formula88||04-07-2001||01:48 AM||||First, check all your fuses.  (I assume there's gas in the tank - always double-check).  Then check the codes on the computer, if any.  If you aren't getting a Service Engine Soon light when you first turn the key to on (engine still off), then either the bulbs burnt out or the ECM is not coming on.  That's what happened to my Formula.  No voltage to the ECM.  It would crank all day, and fuel pressure was perfect, but the injectors wouldn't fire.  Start there and let us know what you find.||||reg||3
Z||000006||Wolfhound||04-07-2001||07:58 AM||||Formula88, I put 2.5 gallons of gas in after replacing the fuel pump. Service engine soon light comes on with ignition. It cranks in the start position and when I release the key it goes dead. I,ll check for codes this morning.<BR> <BR> fyerstarter, fuel pump is running, and it,s showing slightly over 40psi at the shrader, I can hear it, even after it stops running. oil pressure runs 70psi cold. <P> I had worked with the car all day, maybe it will be simple to see this morning. sometimes it helps to get away for a while.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Wolfhound||04-07-2001||10:12 AM||||Josh, Yes I did get the money order, thanks.<P>All fuses are good, and nothing but clear 1-2 1-2 1-2 on the computer. The mystery continues ?||||reg||1
Z||000008||MrPBody||04-07-2001||02:04 PM||||So it sounds like you're getting spark and fuel when you're cranking but not with the switch in "Run" position. . . ?<P>Back in the days when cars had coil resistors (back in the days when distributors had points) I would guess that you have a bad coil resistor.  Now, I don't know.<P>Is there a different supply path for ignition or fuel pump power when cranking <I>vs.</I> running?  Maybe an oil pressure switch that interrupts power to the fuel pump when oil pressure goes away?  Sorta' guessing here.<P>Good luck, anyhow!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Wolfhound||04-07-2001||03:02 PM||||It seems that maybe the cold start injector is supplying enough gas to crank it but then when it switches to the main injectors it quits? Just changed the fuel filter with no result. I,ve got in my mind that it,s electrical, guess I,LL try a few more test. <BR>the pressure switch should be OK unless it,s failing in some odd manner. I can here the pump when it goes dead.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Wolfhound||04-07-2001||04:41 PM||||Friggin mice!!!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mice.JPG"> <BR>Mice had found their way behind the consol through the drivers side firewall connector through hole which was missing it,s fastner. About 4 wires are cut, Time to go solder. It was giving no codes just 1-2 1-2 Guess it was happy to be on vacation  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000011||Wolfhound||04-07-2001||06:55 PM||||"Bingo" Cranked fist shot after soldering the wires back together. How it ran to begin with I have no clue? Idled about 10 minutes and the belt kasploded. replaced that with my GT,s spare and it runs good.<BR>Thanks for the suggestions!||||reg||1
